    "credit": "EatWithAishwarya",
    "notes": "No speech (music only) and no amounts or text on screen, so all amounts are my estimates from what is shown. The video is a lunchbox POV: the veg is cooked quickly, the green sauce is blended and poured over, and the box is packed with a side of rice (the rice cooking is not shown, so rice is optional). Which seasonings were used is read from the shakers (green cap looks like oregano or mixed herbs, orange cap chilli flakes). Pale green cubes look like zucchini; thin green pieces like French beans. After the first pour, a second creamy white liquid is poured in (more milk or the rest of the sauce, not clear). Cooking time and flame level are not shown. The blending itself is not shown: the blend step uses the full jar and the finished sauce. Pesto-style sauce: basil, paneer, garlic, green chilli, cheese and milk."
